# RDLC Audience Firewall Configuration
#
# Per-deliverable forbidden patterns. The audience-firewall.sh hook reads this
# file when Write/Edit/MultiEdit fires on output/ paths.
#
# Format (one rule per line):
#   <deliverable-glob>|<forbidden-pattern>|<reason>
#
# - deliverable-glob: shell-style glob matching the file path (e.g. output/public_*.html)
# - forbidden-pattern: ERE regex (case-insensitive) — the content the deliverable must not contain
# - reason: human-readable explanation surfaced when the gate trips
#
# Comment lines start with #. Empty lines ignored.

# --- Examples (delete or customize for your project) ---

# Public-facing deliverables must not contain salary figures from private prep
# output/public_*.html|salary range|salary figures belong to private interview prep only
# output/public_*.html|\$1[01]\d,\d{3}|specific salary numbers leak from private deliverable

# Clinical PDFs must not contain litigation-style language
# output/clinical_*.pdf|smoking gun|litigation language inappropriate for clinical audience
# output/clinical_*.pdf|manufacturer.{0,20}negligen|manufacturer claims belong to bottle-evidence litigation page

# Family-facing pages must not contain clinical jargon
# output/family_*.html|GRADE: (Very Low|Low|Moderate|High)|GRADE labels belong on clinician pages

